    {
      "id": "claim_1a64a163e2a84597bbe4a523d838db03",
      "statement": "`PreparedCitationCorpus.from_sources` takes the Rust prepare path when `use_rust=True` (the default), `cite_right._core` imports successfully, the tokenizer is a `SimpleTokenizer`, and the source segmenter is a `SimpleSegmenter`. When any condition fails the Python prepare path runs and the resulting corpus has `inverted_index=None` and `rust_corpus=None`, so `_select_candidates` falls back to lexical prefilter.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1189-L1216",
